.TH GIT-EACH "1" "February 2026" "eulegang" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-each \- broadcast commands to git repositories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git each
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,COMMAND\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP

Find all git repositories under a directory, run a command and report process outcomes according to a format.

The command may be git oriented or a system level command.

Each command that is run has \fBGIT_EACH_DIR\fP set to the relative (to the directory this command was run from) dir the command was run on.

The format is specified in the git-each-format page.

.TP
\fB-d, --directory DIR\fP
search for git repositories under DIR. defaults to the current working directory.

.TP
\fB-s, --system\fP
the command is a system one instead of git oriented

.TP
\fB-D, --discover\fP
just search and print repositories (do not run an action)

.TP
\fB-j, --jobs N\fP
the amount of threads to run while processing the commands

.TP
\fB-f, --format FORMAT\fP
the format of the report after a command has finished.
see git-each-format for more information.

.TP
\fB-F, --file FILE\fP
a script to execute instead of a running a command

.TP
\fB-I, --interpreter INTERP\fP
an interpreter to run the `SCRIPT`. by default uses `SHELL`

